# LEGAL-005: Intellectual Property Policy

## INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY POLICY
**MedSync Health**
**Document ID:** LEGAL-005
**Version:** 1.0
**Effective Date:** January 1, 2026
**Prepared by:** Office of the General Counsel (Robert Foster)
**Location:** Boston, MA, USA

---

## 1. PURPOSE AND SCOPE

### 1.1 Purpose
The purpose of this Intellectual Property Policy (the "Policy") is to establish clear guidelines regarding the ownership, protection, and use of Intellectual Property (IP) created, developed, or used by employees, contractors, consultants, and other personnel (collectively, "Personnel") of **MedSync Health** (the "Company"). As a leading Healthcare Technology / Digital Health Platform, the Company's IP is its most valuable asset, essential to its competitive advantage and continued success.

### 1.2 Scope
This Policy applies to all Personnel, regardless of their employment status, location (including Boston, MA, London, UK, Berlin, Germany, and Singapore offices), or role within the Company. It covers all IP created or conceived during the term of their relationship with the Company, whether or not during working hours, that relates to the Company's actual or anticipated business, research, or development.

---

## 2. DEFINITIONS

**2.1 Intellectual Property (IP):** Any and all inventions, discoveries, designs, formulas, know-how, trade secrets, technical data, computer software (including source code and object code), algorithms, databases, processes, methods, works of authorship, trademarks, service marks, trade dress, and all related rights, whether or not patentable, copyrightable, or registrable.

**2.2 Company IP:** All IP that is owned by **MedSync Health** or that the Company has the right to use or license. This includes, but is not limited to, the IP embodied in **MedSync Connect**, **MedSync Analytics**, **MedSync Patient Portal**, and **MedSync Compliance Suite** products.

**2.3 Assigned IP:** Any IP conceived, created, developed, or reduced to practice by Personnel, either alone or jointly with others, during the period of their relationship with the Company, that (a) relates to the Company's business, or (b) is developed using Company time, equipment, supplies, or Confidential Information.

**2.4 Confidential Information:** Non-public information relating to the Company's business, including trade secrets, financial data, customer lists, product roadmaps, and technical specifications. (See **SEC-001** for the full **Security and Confidentiality Policy**).

---

## 3. OWNERSHIP AND ASSIGNMENT

### 3.1 Automatic Assignment
All Personnel agree that all Assigned IP shall be the sole and exclusive property of **MedSync Health**. Personnel hereby irrevocably assign to the Company all right, title, and interest in and to all Assigned IP.

### 3.2 Works Made for Hire
To the extent any Assigned IP qualifies as a "work made for hire" under applicable copyright law, it is hereby deemed a work made for hire for the Company. To the extent any Assigned IP does not qualify as a work made for hire, this Policy serves as the express assignment of all rights, title, and interest in such IP to the Company.

### 3.3 Execution of Documents
Personnel agree to execute any and all applications, assignments, or other instruments that the Company deems necessary to obtain, perfect, vest, maintain, or enforce the Company's rights in the Assigned IP, including patents, copyrights, and trademark registrations, both in the United States and in foreign countries.

---

## 4. PRIOR INVENTIONS

### 4.1 Disclosure of Prior Inventions
Personnel must disclose in writing to the General Counsel (Robert Foster) any IP that they conceived or reduced to practice prior to their relationship with the Company ("Prior Inventions") that they wish to exclude from the scope of Assigned IP.

### 4.2 Company Use of Prior Inventions
If, in the course of their relationship with the Company, Personnel incorporate a Prior Invention into any Company product, process, or service, they are deemed to grant the Company a non-exclusive, royalty-free, perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, sublicensable license to make, use, sell, and otherwise exploit such Prior Invention as part of the Company IP.

---

## 5. PROTECTION OF COMPANY IP

### 5.1 Confidentiality Obligations
Personnel must treat all Confidential Information and trade secrets of the Company with the highest degree of care and must not disclose, publish, or use such information except as required in the performance of their duties for the Company. This obligation survives the termination of the relationship.

### 5.2 Compliance with Security Policy
Personnel must adhere to all protocols and procedures outlined in the Company's **Security and Confidentiality Policy (SEC-001)**, which governs the handling, storage, and transmission of all Company data, including IP and Confidential Information. Furthermore, all IP handling must comply with relevant certifications, including **SOC 2 Type II**, **HIPAA**, **ISO 27001**, and **GDPR Compliance** standards.

### 5.3 Documentation and Record-Keeping
Personnel are required to maintain complete and accurate records of all Assigned IP, including the date of conception, development process, and reduction to practice. These records shall be the exclusive property of the Company.

---

## 6. THIRD-PARTY INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY

### 6.1 Respect for Third-Party Rights
Personnel must respect the IP rights of third parties. The unauthorized copying, use, or distribution of third-party software, documentation, or other copyrighted materials is strictly prohibited.

### 6.2 Open Source Software
The use of Open Source Software (OSS) must comply with the Company's internal OSS Review and Approval Process. Personnel must ensure that the use of any OSS does not create any obligation for the Company to disclose its proprietary source code or otherwise compromise the Company's ownership of its Assigned IP.

---

## 7. POLICY ADMINISTRATION AND ENFORCEMENT

### 7.1 Administration
This Policy is administered by the General Counsel, Robert Foster, who is responsible for interpreting the Policy and overseeing its enforcement.

### 7.2 Violations
Any violation of this Policy may result in disciplinary action, up to and including immediate termination of employment or contract, and may subject the Personnel to legal action for damages and injunctive relief.

---

## ACKNOWLEDGEMENT

By accepting or continuing a relationship with **MedSync Health**, all Personnel acknowledge that they have read, understood, and agree to comply with all terms and conditions set forth in this Intellectual Property Policy.

